  "description": "WEHFUM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C139 H127 Dy7 N10 O31,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.723-3.922 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.00-114.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy7(OH)2(L')9(aib)]·4MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
